    "description": "Digital Information Technologies Corporation operates as an information services company. The company focuses on commissioned development projects for end-users and information systems in various fields, including finance, pharmaceuticals, telecommunications, distribution, transportation, manufacturing, and the public sector. Its products include WebARGUS, a website security solution; xoBlos, a platform for Excel, which automates inefficient Excel-based tasks; DD-CONNECT, an outsourcing service for electronic contracts. The company also develops embedded systems development business, software for automotive devices, mobile devices, consumer electronics, and communication equipment; and offers verification services, including various laboratory tests. In addition, it sells Data Migration Box, a data migration tool; PDF-Xchange series, PDF integration software; USB memory stick type data erasure software; as well as system sales business. Digital Information Technologies Corporation was founded in 1982 and is headquartered in Chuo, Japan."
